Subject: [PATCH 3/3] 3-a-day call cadence and automatic GHL stage advancement

Cadence: 6 calls/day on 2-hour intervals -> 3/day, one per window
(9-11am, 1-4pm, 5-7pm) in the lead's local time. Double-tap off; the
next window is the retry. max_calls 42 -> 21.

Stages: advance_sequence_stage() walks the opportunity forward on every
attempt and jumps it to a terminal stage on outcome. Stage names are
tried as an alias list so one code path drives the English 'Solar Leads
Client' board and the Spanish 'DENVER 1' board.

SEQUENCE_PIPELINE_NAME pins the pipeline - 'Appointment Set' exists in
six pipelines in this location and an unpinned search can move a card
into the wrong funnel.

Also: appointments now carry the address in the appointment's own address
field (verified empty on the one booked appointment in GHL) plus bill and
homeowner status in the notes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
